  ],
  "notes": "A craft and industry term; the kanji form is {鞣|なめ}す. ⟦{皮|かわ}→皮：02187_kawa⟧ is the raw hide; after tanning it becomes ⟦{革|かわ}→革：19310_kawa⟧ (leather).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{皮|かわ}→皮：02187_kawa⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧なめす: to tan a hide\n- なめし{革|がわ}: tanned leather\n- ⟦{植物|しょくぶつ}→植物：03248_shokubutsu⟧タンニンなめし: vegetable tanning\n\nWATCH OUT:\nDo not confuse with ⟦{舐|な}める→舐める：04399_nameru⟧ (to lick), which shares the sound な but is an ichidan verb.",
